<!--
********** The Lead Capture Visualforce page **********

This Visualforce page simply loads the Lead Capture web UI in an iframe. This allows us to make Lead Capture
look like it's a native Salesforce feature even though the code (apart from this page) is entirely hosted 
on our servers.

To setup / modify this page:

1. Login to the appropriate Developer Edition Salesforce org for the environment you're working on
(see the Lead Capture doc site for the list of Dev Ed orgs we use: https://github.exacttarget.com/pages/ad-studio/lead-ingestion/salescloud-accounts.html)

2. Make sure that you've already added the SalesforceLeadCaptureController Apex class to the org. If not,
do it first (see the LeadCaptureVisualforceController.apex file).  

3. In Classic Experience, navigate to Setup -> Build -> Develop -> Visualforce Pages.
Visualforce pages can also be edited in Lightning Experience. Where to find them there is left as an exercise to the reader.

4. Add / Edit the page. IMPORTANT: make sure to change the URL of the Lead Capture web UI to the correct one depending on your environment.

Our Visualforce page is included in our AppExchange Package - it gets automatically added to the customer's org when they install our package.
 
-->

<apex:page sidebar="false" controller="sfleadcaphfprod.SalesforceLeadCaptureController" >
    <style type="text/css">
         .brandQuaternaryBgr {
             padding: 0px !important;
         }
         
         .fullPage iframe {
             width: 100%;
             height: 100%;
             min-height: 600px;
             padding: 0;
             margin: 0;
         }

         html, .fullPage {
             height: 100%;
         }
     </style>
    <div class="fullPage">

        <!-- 
            The !$ variables are global variables. 
            The full list of global variables accessible from a Visualforce page can be found here: 
            https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.pages.meta/pages/pages_variables_global.htm

            The ! variables (i.e. those without the $) are properties of our custom controller (SalesforceLeadCaptureController).
            This controller is just an Apex class that you'll find in the Setup -> Build -> Develop -> Apex Classes section. 
        -->

        <apex:iframe height="100%" width="100%" src="https://leadcap-01.social.com/_command/salescloud/login?orgId={!URLENCODE($Organization.Id)}&orgName={!URLENCODE($Organization.Name)}&isSandbox={!isSandbox}&userId={!URLENCODE($User.Id)}&username={!URLENCODE($User.Username)}&entrepriseServerUrl={!URLENCODE($Api.Enterprise_Server_URL_370)}" scrolling="true" />
    </div>
</apex:page>